---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { contact } from "@apricot/brand";

const updated = "14 October 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · Apricot Stays"
  description="How Apricot Stays handles personal data on apricotstays.in and in WhatsApp enquiries, in line with India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="wrap">
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Your privacy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This notice explains what personal data Apricot Stays ("we") handles through
        <strong>apricotstays.in</strong> and when you contact us on WhatsApp. It is written to meet
        India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act).
      </p>

      <h2>What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing that identifies you.</strong> There are no forms, no accounts, no cookies
        and no advertising or tracking pixels. Fonts are served from our own site, so your browser
        does not contact Google or other font services.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Visitor statistics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page
          views and page speed without cookies, without storing IP addresses and without building
          visitor profiles.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Security logs.</strong> Our host, Cloudflare, briefly processes technical data
          such as IP address and browser type to deliver the site and block attacks.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>When you message us on WhatsApp</h2>
      <p>
        If you tap "Chat on WhatsApp", you choose to start a conversation with us on WhatsApp, a
        service run by Meta under its own privacy policy. We use what you send us — typically your
        name, phone number, dates and number of guests — <strong>only</strong> to answer your
        enquiry and, if you book, to arrange and manage your stay.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell your data or use it for advertising. We keep enquiry chats only as long as we
        need them for your enquiry or stay, and booking records for as long as Indian law requires
        (for example, for tax and guest-registration rules).
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the DPDP Act you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what personal data we hold about you and how we use it;</li>
        <li>correct, complete or update it;</li>
        <li>erase it, where we no longer need to keep it;</li>
        <li>withdraw any consent you have given; and</li>
        <li>nominate someone to exercise these rights for you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact and grievances</h2>
      <p>
        Message us on WhatsApp at <a href="https://wa.me/919740544873">{contact.whatsappDisplay}</a>
        or email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>. We will respond as soon as
        we can and within the time the law allows. If you are not satisfied with our response, you
        can complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we start collecting more data — for example through an enquiry or booking form — we will
        update this notice first and ask for your consent where required.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style is:global>
  body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .wrap {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1160px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }
  main {
    flex: 1;
    padding: 24px 24px 72px;
  }
  article {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--apricot-text);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.5vw, 64px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
  }
  article p,
  article li {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  article p + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  article strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  article ul {
    margin: 14px 0 0 1.2em;
  }
  article li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  article a {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .wrap,
    main {
      padding-left: 16px;
      padding-right: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
